      "section": "type",
      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/places/places.en.ts",
      "line": 26,
      "purpose": "ALREADY CHOSEN, reopenable.  That's all a type says:  from then on, a recipe you add or change is kept there, with no save step.",
      "note": "Today:\n\nA (built, recommended):  `- it is saved in the family cookbook`  --  chosen by you (Q1).  Spell already says `is saved in its own file`\n\nB:  `- it is kept in the family cookbook`  --  the most natural English, with no hint of a step to do.  A second word for nearly one idea.\n\nC:  `- it comes from the family cookbook`  --  how Bubble and Retool say it, but nobody expects to write to where something comes from.\n\nD:  `- it lives in the family cookbook`  --  your words at the kickoff.\n\nWhy:  Decided.  What the parser found:  only a place's name may follow, or `is saved in its own file` reads `its own` as a property.\n\nRenaming it later:  86 lines in 33 files of rules, tests and docs, 9 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "- it is saved in the family cookbook",
      "recommended": "- it is saved in the family cookbook"
    },
    {
      "id": "every",
      "section": "read",
      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/classes/classes.en.ts",
      "line": 2251,
      "purpose": "All of them.  For a saved type, this now means all those in the place, not a scratch list of what the program made.",
      "note": "Today:  Runs:  the recipe box.  `the recipes` means the same, and is the plural form.\n\nA (built, recommended):  `every recipe`  --  the old word, reaching further.  One word tells one from many, as AppleScript's `every window` does.\n\nB:  `all recipes`  --  everyday too\n\nC:  `all the recipes`  --  the most spoken form, and one more word.\n\nWhy:  Keep the English, which every Spell program already reads.\n\nRenaming it later:  1232 lines in 423 files of rules, tests and docs, 282 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "every recipe",
      "recommended": "every recipe"
    },
    {
      "id": "where",
      "section": "read",
      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/classes/classes.en.ts",
      "line": 2275,
      "purpose": "Only the ones that fit.  Compiled so the place does the filtering when it can.",
      "note": "Today:  A condition the place can't answer, like this one, warns  and is worked out on the page.\n\nA (built, recommended):  `every recipe where its title includes the search`  --  Spell already used it (`the items in x where`), and it needs no verb first, unlike Bubble's `Do a search for`.\n\nB:  `every recipe whose title includes the search`  --  AppleScript's word, and elegant, but `whose` fits only a property, not `where it is quick`.\n\nC:  `every recipe that includes the search in its title`  --  the most spoken form, and every condition would need its own wording.\n\nWhy:  One word that fits every condition.  `the recipes where ...`, which the first proposal also listed, doesn't compile:  only `every recipe where`.\n\nRenaming it later:  789 lines in 314 files of rules, tests and docs, 133 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "every recipe where its title includes the search",
      "recommended": "every recipe where its title includes the search"
    },
    {
      "id": "sorted-by",
      "section": "read",
      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/lists/lists.en.ts",
      "line": 544,
      "purpose": "In order of something about each one.  The place does it when it can.",
      "note": "Today:\n\nA (built, recommended):  `every recipe, sorted by its title`  --  what spreadsheets say (Sort).\n\nB:  `every recipe, ordered by its title`  --  SQL's word in English.\n\nC:  `every recipe, in order of its title`  --  reads aloud well  Longer.\n\nWhy:  and warns when one disagrees with its list.  The other way round (`from highest to lowest`) is proposed  and not built.\n\nRenaming it later:  21 lines in 11 files of rules, tests and docs, 2 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "every recipe, sorted by its title",
      "recommended": "every recipe, sorted by its title"
    },
    {
