      "purpose": "The oldest one:  first made, or, for a saved type, first in the place's order.",
      "note": "Today:  Runs:  an old word that reaches further.\n\nA (built, recommended):  `the first recipe`  --  one word for one thing, and no new word.\n\nB:  `the oldest recipe`  --  says what it means for a saved type, and reads as a sort that isn't there.\n\nC:  `the earliest recipe`  --  exact, and rarely said.\n\nWhy:  The old word still means first in its order.\n\nRenaming it later:  4 lines in 3 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "the first recipe",
