      "purpose": "What to draw when the read comes back empty.",
      "note": "Today:\n\nA (built, recommended):  `if there are none:`  --  the sentence a person would say.\n\nB:  `if there aren't any:`  --  more spoken.  but it's clipped.\n\nC:  `if it is empty:`  --  a programmer's way to see it.  TRAP:  it compiles today, to a test of the program itself, not of the list.\n\nWhy:  and warns if it doesn't.\n\nRenaming it later:  9 lines in 8 files of rules, tests and docs, 2 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "if there are none:",
