      "purpose": "What to draw when the read doesn't work.  Write nothing, and it shows a message with Try again.",
      "note": "Today:\n\nA (built, recommended):  `if that fails:`  --  `that`, since `it` is already the outline's thing.\n\nB:  `if it fails:`  --  more natural, and `it` would mean the wrong thing inside a type.\n\nC:  `if it doesn't work:`  --  the plainest words, and has the same trouble with `it`.\n\nWhy:\n\nRenaming it later:  9 lines in 8 files of rules, tests and docs, 2 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "if that fails:",
