      "section": "named",
      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/places/OperationAt.ts",
      "line": 12,
      "purpose": "How to declare something a place can do beyond add, change and remove.  THIS ROW ANSWERS Q17.",
      "note": "Today:  NEITHER COMPILES on the real parser today.  B fails on its address.  A is what's built  and the action reads  only the prototype's test parser reads it.  Written here on one line:  in a program, A's detail is indented under the action.\n\nA (built, recommended):  `- to publish (a recipe):  - it is at \"/recipes/publish\"`  --  two lines per operation, and no change to how an action is read;  it can take the details any action takes, as `- undone as` does.\n\nB:  `- to publish (a recipe) is at \"/recipes/publish\"`  --  one line, but `to ...` would have to learn to stop at `is at`, so a program's action with those words in its name changes meaning.\n\nWhy:  A, as built.  Either way the rule needs fixing:  no test covers it on the real parser.\n\nRenaming it later:  2 lines in 2 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
